  "evidence": "Mimecast's help centre says Directory Synchronization lets you 'securely automate the management of Mimecast users and groups using your company directory' (LDAP/AD, Azure AD, Google Workspace, Domino); no SCIM endpoint is documented for Email Security.",
  "notes": "Quote-only: Email Security plans (Critical, Advanced, Premium) are all Contact Sales, so price fields are null. Researched the main admin product (Mimecast Email Security / Administration Console): users are managed by Mimecast-run directory sync from on-prem AD (LDAP or Synchronization Engine), Microsoft Entra (Azure AD), Google Workspace or Domino, syncing three times daily; there is no SCIM. Admin SSO is SAML via Authentication Profiles; Entra lists a Mimecast gallery app for SSO only. Mimecast's Incydr (ex-Code42) insider-risk product separately supports inbound SCIM 2.0 from Okta, Entra and PingOne; that is not scored here. API 1.0 (regional hosts) can create cloud users via /api/user/create-user; plan gate not stated.",
